 * The Callable does virtually no work to isolate the overhead of the RxJava machinery.
 *
 * Best practices applied:
 * - Use @State(Scope.Thread) to avoid sharing mutable state between threads.
 * - Initialize the Completable once in @Setup to exclude construction cost from the benchmark.
 * - Use Blackhole to consume possible errors and prevent dead‑code elimination.
 * - Configure warm‑up, measurement iterations and forks for reliable results.
